                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fbe20f05-0cea-381f-82b5-003c8c7779b6",
                        "entry_id": "58efbb9d-feac-3dc8-b814-72cb885f764e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "schwefelsaures Doppelsalz meist von Kalium oder Aluminium, das zum Beizen, Färben und zum Stillen von Blutungen verwendet wird"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a414eb2-e17a-43c5-b14b-c3ecad56b85f",
                                "sense_id": "fbe20f05-0cea-381f-82b5-003c8c7779b6",
                                "text": "„Dafür erwies sich Alaun als Mittel der Wahl.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cc1e6fc-35c5-47e9-a695-3e36fe22c3e2",
                                "sense_id": "fbe20f05-0cea-381f-82b5-003c8c7779b6",
                                "text": "„Danach mußten sich die löslichen Substanzen, schwefelsaures Eisen und Alaun, von den unlöslichen, Kieselerde, verbrannte Kohle und Asche, getrennt haben.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77a04fb6-0485-4a1b-8ceb-45487be74a7b",
                        "source_entry_id": "58efbb9d-feac-3dc8-b814-72cb885f764e",
                        "source_sense_id": "fbe20f05-0cea-381f-82b5-003c8c7779b6",
                        "source_sense_description": "schwefelsaures Doppelsalz",
                        "target_lang_word": "alum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21589e45-7674-3d1c-8f25-eb200b0f6d41",
                                        "entry_id": "d7610614-c344-3990-bfca-9de572a175b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An astringent salt, usually occurring in the form of pale crystals, much used in the dyeing and tanning trade and in certain medicines, and now understood to be a double sulphate of potassium and aluminium (K₂SO₄·Al₂(SO₄)₃·24H₂O)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5bba657-afc3-437c-96e9-46e9fb446c92",
                                                "sense_id": "21589e45-7674-3d1c-8f25-eb200b0f6d41",
                                                "text": "Venice also needed alum for trade, since it was the point of departure for overland transportation of alum to southern Germany and its cloth-manufacturing Free Cities."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfe3bdad-fb9b-4424-8203-7676ae044935",
                                                "sense_id": "21589e45-7674-3d1c-8f25-eb200b0f6d41",
                                                "text": "A natural astringent and antiseptic, potassium alum was coveted for its medicinal and cosmetic properties."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a92a9d1-d35b-32ca-82a5-cc8d79740a6c",
                                        "entry_id": "d7610614-c344-3990-bfca-9de572a175b2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any similar double sulphate in which either or both of the potassium and aluminium is wholly or partly replaced by other univalent or tervalent cations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a727a83-70ec-4c89-b312-2960243379eb",
                                                "sense_id": "0a92a9d1-d35b-32ca-82a5-cc8d79740a6c",
                                                "text": "With weld and cochineal, which are colouring matters the most sensible to the action of sulphate of iron, the purified alums gave us colours more brilliant, fresh, and in a slight degree lighter; while those with our common alums were all duller, and evidently of a deeper hue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41a338d2-72b3-477f-9311-5a1c07438163",
                                                "sense_id": "0a92a9d1-d35b-32ca-82a5-cc8d79740a6c",
                                                "text": "For similar reasons, aluminium sulphate and alums are used in dyeing cloth.[…]Normally alums are soluble in water and insoluble in alcohols."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1fd27ff-7d4c-42cc-881b-303c78cbfa8f",
                                                "sense_id": "0a92a9d1-d35b-32ca-82a5-cc8d79740a6c",
                                                "text": "In structure, the alums consist of simple ions, being not complexes, but double salts. Potash alum or potassium alum is the common alum, with the formula KAl(SO₄)₂·12H₂O) which, for convenience, may be written K₂SO₄·Al₂(SO₄)₃·24H₂O"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "alum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5d7612a-ad1b-3078-8f9a-ebe4045d251f",
                                        "entry_id": "08a88675-357e-3107-b864-b67a6eb3a6ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To steep in, or otherwise impregnate with, a solution of alum; to treat with alum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dde234a5-8ea7-45f9-ae21-041ebe391be6",
                                                "sense_id": "e5d7612a-ad1b-3078-8f9a-ebe4045d251f",
                                                "text": "The silk should be boiled at the rate of 20 parts of soap per cent. , and then alumed. The aluming need not be so strong as for the fine crimson"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3db0cec8-2ab1-4cc2-9a52-0f635f548058",
                                                "sense_id": "e5d7612a-ad1b-3078-8f9a-ebe4045d251f",
                                                "text": "After drying, the cloth was alumed and finally dyed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "alum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34e9c59d-3238-3322-87fb-e8091158bbb7",
                                        "entry_id": "770785e0-5850-304b-b786-7be1cc6aa330",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A past attendee or graduate (of any gender) of a college, university or other educational institution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bcac95b-dcaa-4916-90e8-863521c199d9",
                                                "sense_id": "34e9c59d-3238-3322-87fb-e8091158bbb7",
                                                "text": "1961 Spring, Anchora of Delta Gamma, Volume LXXVII, No. 3, page 59,\nEvanston-North Shore alums are happy to open their homes to Sigma actives for special social events."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9e15bf6-c20d-4999-9e21-5e25ad67186e",
                                                "sense_id": "34e9c59d-3238-3322-87fb-e8091158bbb7",
                                                "text": "You'll remember that we're starting with a list of slightly over 7,000 names that are alums (most of them over 50) that we'd like to whittle down to a manageable list of prospects."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4123c4dc-e1c4-4647-9eae-f3fdb4cce95f",
                                                "sense_id": "34e9c59d-3238-3322-87fb-e8091158bbb7",
                                                "text": "All schools that last have alums, and, ancient as it was by American standards, Trinity by mid-century had thousands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb5795c5-3490-4fb4-9c25-4ee6815f21ad",
                                                "sense_id": "34e9c59d-3238-3322-87fb-e8091158bbb7",
                                                "text": "“It breaks my heart to see them naked, undignified, shivering in the cold as they swallow our daily filth,” proclaims the woman, played by the Saturday Night Live alum Aidy Bryant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e64cd405-c852-484b-8c79-33dc519ab035",
                        "source_entry_id": "58efbb9d-feac-3dc8-b814-72cb885f764e",
                        "source_sense_id": "fbe20f05-0cea-381f-82b5-003c8c7779b6",
